IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-logic`

-- SECTION 2016a, EBT BENEFIT FRAUD PREVENTION (7 U.S.C. 2016a): lines 1201-1259 of usc07-ch51.txt.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE NUMBER, MAYBE DATE) with: JUST TRUE = the text says yes;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say. Money is a NUMBER of dollars.
-- A duty without a stated time is answered "has done": JUST TRUE if done, NOTHING if not.
-- Source is a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

-- WHAT SECTION 2016a(b)(2) SAYS ABOUT ONE REPLACEMENT of benefits stolen by card skimming, card cloning or a similar method. A number cannot say "no", so the answer is a constructor.
DECLARE `s 2016a(b)(2) replacement` IS ONE OF
    `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` HAS `the most the replacement may be, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section`
    `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`

-- THE DATES section 2016a counts from, taken from its words.
-- src:1225 | not later than 60 days after December 29, 2022
@ref s 2016a(b)(1) the date from which the 60 days for submitting the plan are counted (src:1225)
`s 2016a(b)(1) the date from which the 60 days for submitting the plan are counted` MEANS Date 29 12 2022

-- 29 December 2022 and 60 days: 2 days to 31 December, 31 to 31 January, 27 to 27 February 2023.
`s 2016a(b)(1) the last day for submitting the plan` MEANS Date (Day `s 2016a(b)(1) the date from which the 60 days for submitting the plan are counted` PLUS 60)

-- src:1241 | beginning on October 1, 2022, and ending on December 20, 2024
@ref s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the first day of the period of theft covered (src:1241)
`s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the first day of the period of theft covered` MEANS Date 1 10 2022

`s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the last day of the period of theft covered` MEANS Date 20 12 2024

-- src:1209 | not later than December 1, 2023
@ref s 2016a(a)(3) the last day for promulgating the regulations (src:1209)
`s 2016a(a)(3) the last day for promulgating the regulations` MEANS Date 1 12 2023

-- src:1217 | not later than December 1, 2024
@ref s 2016a(a)(5) the last day for submitting the report (src:1217)
`s 2016a(a)(5) the last day for submitting the report` MEANS Date 1 12 2024

-- src:1250 | Not later than 1 year after September 26, 2024
@ref s 2016a(e)(1) the date from which the year for the Comptroller General's report is counted (src:1250)
`s 2016a(e)(1) the date from which the year for the Comptroller General's report is counted` MEANS Date 26 9 2024

`s 2016a(e)(1) the last day for the Comptroller General's report` MEANS `add years` `s 2016a(e)(1) the date from which the year for the Comptroller General's report is counted` 1

-- src:1247 | Of the unobligated balances made available for the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program as authorized by section 1101(b)(1) of the American Rescue Plan Act of 2021 (Public Law 117–2), $8,000,000 is hereby rescinded.
@ref s 2016a(d) the amount rescinded is $8,000,000 (src:1247)
`s 2016a(d) the amount of the unobligated balances rescinded, in dollars` MEANS 8000000

§ `s 2016a -- EBT benefit fraud prevention`

§§ `s 2016a(a) guidance and rulemaking`

-- src:1209 | (3) not later than December 1, 2023, promulgate regulations (including an interim final rule) to require State agencies to implement procedures for the replacement of benefits consistent with subsection (b);
@ref s 2016a(a)(3) the Secretary promulgates regulations by 1 December 2023 requiring State agencies to implement replacement procedures consistent with subsection (b) (src:1209)
GIVEN `the date on which the Secretary promulgated the regulations` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(a)(3) the Secretary promulgated the regulations in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the Secretary promulgated the regulations`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no date was supplied, and whether the Secretary has promulgated the regulations yet depends on today's date, which the text does not give
            NOTHING
        WHEN JUST promulgated THEN
            IF Day promulgated AT MOST Day `s 2016a(a)(3) the last day for promulgating the regulations`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than December 1, 2023, promulgate regulations (including an interim final rule)"
                JUST FALSE

-- src:1210 | (4) coordinate with the Administrator of the Administration for Children and Families of the Department of Health and Human Services, the Attorney General of the United States, State agencies, retail food stores, and EBT contractors—
-- src:1211 | (A) to determine—
-- src:1212 | (i) how benefits are being stolen through card skimming, card cloning, and other similar fraudulent methods;
-- src:1213 | (ii) how those stolen benefits are used; and
-- src:1214 | (iii) the locations where card skimming, card cloning, and other similar fraudulent methods are taking place;
-- src:1215 | (B) to establish measures, including equipment enhancements for retail food stores, to prevent benefits from being stolen through card skimming, card cloning, and other similar fraudulent methods; and
-- src:1216 | (C) to establish standard reporting methods for States to collect and share data with the Secretary on the scope of benefits being stolen through card skimming, card cloning, and other similar fraudulent methods; and
@ref s 2016a(a)(4) the Secretary coordinates with the named bodies to determine how benefits are stolen, to establish measures, and to establish standard reporting methods (src:1210-1216)
GIVEN `the Secretary has coordinated with the Administrator of the Administration for Children and Families of the Department of Health and Human Services, the Attorney General of the United States, State agencies, retail food stores, and EBT contractors to do what subparagraphs (A), (B) and (C) describe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(a)(4) the Secretary has done what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has coordinated with the Administrator of the Administration for Children and Families of the Department of Health and Human Services, the Attorney General of the United States, State agencies, retail food stores, and EBT contractors to do what subparagraphs (A), (B) and (C) describe` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the Secretary must coordinate
            NOTHING

-- src:1217 | (5) not later than December 1, 2024, submit to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate and the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives a report that includes—
-- src:1218 | (A) information on the frequency of theft of benefits and the location of those thefts, including benefits stolen through card skimming, card cloning, and other similar fraudulent methods;
@ref s 2016a(a)(5) the Secretary reports to the Committees by 1 December 2024 (src:1217-1218)
GIVEN `the date on which the Secretary submitted the report to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate and the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(a)(5) the Secretary submitted the report in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the Secretary submitted the report to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate and the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no date was supplied, and whether the Secretary has submitted the report yet depends on today's date, which the text does not give
            NOTHING
        WHEN JUST submitted THEN
            IF Day submitted AT MOST Day `s 2016a(a)(5) the last day for submitting the report`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than December 1, 2024, submit to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate and the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives a report"
                JUST FALSE

-- src:1217 | (5) not later than December 1, 2024, submit to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate and the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives a report that includes—
-- src:1218 | (A) information on the frequency of theft of benefits and the location of those thefts, including benefits stolen through card skimming, card cloning, and other similar fraudulent methods;
-- src:1219 | (B) a description of the determinations made under paragraph (4)(A), the measures established under paragraph (4)(B), and methods established in paragraph (4)(C);
-- src:1220 | (C) a description of the industry standards described in paragraph (1)(B);
-- src:1221 | (D) a comparison of State plans related to reimbursement, prevention, and other relevant procedures approved in accordance with subsection (b)(1)(A); and
-- src:1222 | (E) recommendations on how to consistently and proactively detect, track, report, and prevent theft of benefits, including benefits stolen through card skimming, card cloning, and other similar fraudulent methods.
@ref s 2016a(a)(5) the report includes the five items listed (src:1217-1222)
GIVEN `the report includes information on the frequency of theft of benefits and the location of those thefts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a description of the determinations made under paragraph (4)(A), the measures established under paragraph (4)(B), and methods established in paragraph (4)(C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a description of the industry standards described in paragraph (1)(B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a comparison of State plans related to reimbursement, prevention, and other relevant procedures approved in accordance with subsection (b)(1)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes recommendations on how to consistently and proactively detect, track, report, and prevent theft of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(a)(5) the report includes what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report includes information on the frequency of theft of benefits and the location of those thefts` AND `the report includes a description of the determinations made under paragraph (4)(A), the measures established under paragraph (4)(B), and methods established in paragraph (4)(C)` AND `the report includes a description of the industry standards described in paragraph (1)(B)` AND `the report includes a comparison of State plans related to reimbursement, prevention, and other relevant procedures approved in accordance with subsection (b)(1)(A)` AND `the report includes recommendations on how to consistently and proactively detect, track, report, and prevent theft of benefits` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "submit to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate and the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives a report that includes"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `s 2016a(b) replacement of benefits`

-- src:1223 | (b) Replacement of benefits
-- src:1224 | The Secretary shall use funds appropriated under section 2027 of this title to require States to replace benefits that are determined by the State agency to have been stolen through card skimming, card cloning, or similar fraudulent methods, subject to the conditions that—
@ref s 2016a(b) the Secretary requires States to replace benefits the State agency determines were stolen by card skimming, card cloning or similar methods (src:1223-1224)
-- In plain words: the Secretary uses funds appropriated under section 2027 to require States to replace benefits that the State agency has determined were stolen through card skimming, card cloning or similar fraudulent methods, on the conditions in paragraphs (1) to (4).
-- This function answers one replacement: how much may be replaced for a household. The terms "allotment", "benefit", "household" and "State agency" have the meaning given in section 2012 (subsection (c)).
GIVEN `s 2012(d) the assistance is a benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(m) the individual or group is a household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(s) the body is a State agency` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has determined that the benefits were stolen through card skimming, card cloning, or similar fraudulent methods` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the benefits were stolen` IS A DATE
      `the amount of benefits stolen from the household, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2012(b) the monthly allotment of the household immediately prior to the date on which the benefits were stolen, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of replacements already made to the household by the State agency in the Federal fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 2016a(b)(2) replacement`
`s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST `s 2012(d) the assistance is a benefit`, `s 2012(m) the individual or group is a household`, `s 2012(s) the body is a State agency`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 2016a(c) gives "allotment", "benefit", "household", "retail food store" and "State agency" the meaning given in section 2012, and the answers were not all supplied
            `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`
        IF Day `the date on which the benefits were stolen` LESS THAN Day `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the first day of the period of theft covered` OR Day `the date on which the benefits were stolen` GREATER THAN Day `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the last day of the period of theft covered` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall only apply to benefits stolen during the period beginning on October 1, 2022, and ending on December 20, 2024"
            `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section`
        IF `the number of replacements already made to the household by the State agency in the Federal fiscal year` AT LEAST 2 THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not occur more than 2 times per Federal fiscal year per household by a single State agency"
            `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section`
        IF NOT (`the State agency has determined that the benefits were stolen through card skimming, card cloning, or similar fraudulent methods` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "benefits that are determined by the State agency to have been stolen through card skimming, card cloning, or similar fraudulent methods"
            `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say`
        OTHERWISE
            -- the cap is the lesser of the amount stolen and two months of the monthly allotment immediately before the theft
            `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` (min `the amount of benefits stolen from the household, in dollars` (2 TIMES `s 2012(b) the monthly allotment of the household immediately prior to the date on which the benefits were stolen, in dollars`))

-- src:1225 | (1) the State agency shall submit to the Secretary not later than 60 days after December 29, 2022, for prior approval a plan for the replacement of stolen benefits that—
-- src:1226 | (A) includes appropriate procedures, as determined by the Secretary, for the timely submission of claims to, timely validation of claims by, and replacement issuance by the State agency that includes—
-- src:1227 | (i) a signed statement by the affected household on the benefit theft, consistent with the signature requirements and options provided by section 2020(e)(2)(C) of this title;
-- src:1228 | (ii) criteria to determine if a submitted claim is valid;
-- src:1229 | (iii) procedures for the documentation of replacement issuances, including the submitted claims and findings from the validation;
-- src:1230 | (iv) the submission of data reports on benefit theft and replacement activity to the Secretary;
-- src:1231 | (v) procedures to inform households of their right to a fair hearing, consistent with those already established by section 2020(e) of this title and corresponding regulations concerning replacement issuances; and
-- src:1232 | (vi) the State agency’s use and planned use of benefit theft prevention measures, including any additional guidance that may be issued under subsection (a)(1);
-- src:1233 | (B) includes appropriate procedures, as determined by the Secretary, for reporting the scope and frequency of card skimming affecting households within the State to the Secretary;
-- src:1234 | (C) upon approval shall be incorporated into the State plan of operation required under section 2020(e) of this title; and
-- src:1235 | (D) the Secretary may approve after the date on which guidance is issued under subsection (a)(1);
-- src:1236 | (2) the replacement of stolen benefits for a household—
-- src:1237 | (A) shall not exceed the lesser of—
-- src:1238 | (i) the amount of benefits stolen from the household; or
-- src:1239 | (ii) the amount equal to 2 months of the monthly allotment of the household immediately prior to the date on which the benefits were stolen;
-- src:1240 | (B) shall not occur more than 2 times per Federal fiscal year per household by a single State agency; and
-- src:1241 | (C) shall only apply to benefits stolen during the period beginning on October 1, 2022, and ending on December 20, 2024;
-- src:1242 | (3) plans approved under paragraph (1) will remain in effect until the effective date of the rule promulgated pursuant to subsection (a)(3); and
-- src:1243 | (4) replacements of benefits under this section shall not be regarded as losses for the purpose of section 2016(e) of this title to the extent such replacements are made in accordance with an approved plan that complies with this subsection.
@ref s 2016a(b)(2)(B) the replacement does not occur more than 2 times per Federal fiscal year per household by a single State agency (src:1225-1243)
GIVEN `the number of replacements already made to the household by the State agency in the Federal fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(2)(B) another replacement may occur in the Federal fiscal year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of replacements already made to the household by the State agency in the Federal fiscal year` AT LEAST 2 THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not occur more than 2 times per Federal fiscal year per household by a single State agency"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not occur more than 2 times"
            -- note (a ceiling: it does not say that a replacement must occur)
            NOTHING

-- src:1241 | (C) shall only apply to benefits stolen during the period beginning on October 1, 2022, and ending on December 20, 2024;
@ref s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the benefits were stolen during the period beginning 1 October 2022 and ending 20 December 2024 (src:1241)
-- In plain words: both the first and the last day of the period count. Benefits stolen on 30 September 2022 or on 21 December 2024 are outside it.
GIVEN `the date on which the benefits were stolen` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the stolen benefits fall within the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF Day `the date on which the benefits were stolen` AT LEAST Day `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the first day of the period of theft covered` AND Day `the date on which the benefits were stolen` AT MOST Day `s 2016a(b)(2)(C) the last day of the period of theft covered` THEN
            -- named for the limit, so inside it the answer is JUST TRUE (both ends count); whether the benefits are then replaced is `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits`, which also asks the other conditions
            JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall only apply to benefits stolen during the period beginning on October 1, 2022, and ending on December 20, 2024"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1225 | (1) the State agency shall submit to the Secretary not later than 60 days after December 29, 2022, for prior approval a plan for the replacement of stolen benefits that—
-- src:1226 | (A) includes appropriate procedures, as determined by the Secretary, for the timely submission of claims to, timely validation of claims by, and replacement issuance by the State agency that includes—
@ref s 2016a(b)(1) the State agency submits its replacement plan not later than 60 days after 29 December 2022 (src:1225-1226)
GIVEN `the date on which the State agency submitted the plan` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(1) the State agency submitted the plan in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF Day `the date on which the State agency submitted the plan` AT MOST Day `s 2016a(b)(1) the last day for submitting the plan` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the State agency shall submit to the Secretary not later than 60 days after December 29, 2022, for prior approval a plan for the replacement of stolen benefits"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1226 | (A) includes appropriate procedures, as determined by the Secretary, for the timely submission of claims to, timely validation of claims by, and replacement issuance by the State agency that includes—
-- src:1227 | (i) a signed statement by the affected household on the benefit theft, consistent with the signature requirements and options provided by section 2020(e)(2)(C) of this title;
-- src:1228 | (ii) criteria to determine if a submitted claim is valid;
-- src:1229 | (iii) procedures for the documentation of replacement issuances, including the submitted claims and findings from the validation;
-- src:1230 | (iv) the submission of data reports on benefit theft and replacement activity to the Secretary;
-- src:1231 | (v) procedures to inform households of their right to a fair hearing, consistent with those already established by section 2020(e) of this title and corresponding regulations concerning replacement issuances; and
-- src:1232 | (vi) the State agency’s use and planned use of benefit theft prevention measures, including any additional guidance that may be issued under subsection (a)(1);
@ref s 2016a(b)(1)(A) the plan includes procedures for timely submission, validation and replacement of claims, with the six items listed (src:1226-1232)
GIVEN `the plan includes a signed statement by the affected household on the benefit theft, consistent with the signature requirements and options provided by section 2020(e)(2)(C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes criteria to determine if a submitted claim is valid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes procedures for the documentation of replacement issuances, including the submitted claims and findings from the validation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes the submission of data reports on benefit theft and replacement activity to the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes procedures to inform households of their right to a fair hearing, consistent with those already established by section 2020(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes the State agency's use and planned use of benefit theft prevention measures, including any additional guidance that may be issued under subsection (a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(1)(A) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the plan includes a signed statement by the affected household on the benefit theft, consistent with the signature requirements and options provided by section 2020(e)(2)(C)` AND `the plan includes criteria to determine if a submitted claim is valid` AND `the plan includes procedures for the documentation of replacement issuances, including the submitted claims and findings from the validation` AND `the plan includes the submission of data reports on benefit theft and replacement activity to the Secretary` AND `the plan includes procedures to inform households of their right to a fair hearing, consistent with those already established by section 2020(e)` AND `the plan includes the State agency's use and planned use of benefit theft prevention measures, including any additional guidance that may be issued under subsection (a)(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a plan for the replacement of stolen benefits that— (A) includes appropriate procedures, as determined by the Secretary, for the timely submission of claims to, timely validation of claims by, and replacement issuance by the State agency that includes"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1233 | (B) includes appropriate procedures, as determined by the Secretary, for reporting the scope and frequency of card skimming affecting households within the State to the Secretary;
@ref s 2016a(b)(1)(B) the plan includes procedures for reporting the scope and frequency of card skimming (src:1233)
GIVEN `the plan includes appropriate procedures, as determined by the Secretary, for reporting the scope and frequency of card skimming affecting households within the State to the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(1)(B) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the plan includes appropriate procedures, as determined by the Secretary, for reporting the scope and frequency of card skimming affecting households within the State to the Secretary`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a plan for the replacement of stolen benefits that"
            -- note (a failed condition; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1234 | (C) upon approval shall be incorporated into the State plan of operation required under section 2020(e) of this title; and
@ref s 2016a(b)(1)(C) the plan, on approval, is incorporated into the State plan of operation (src:1234)
GIVEN `the plan has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan has been incorporated into the State plan of operation required under section 2020(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(1)(C) the plan has been incorporated as the subparagraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the plan has been approved` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon approval shall be incorporated into the State plan of operation"
            NOTHING
        IF `the plan has been incorporated into the State plan of operation required under section 2020(e)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the plan must be incorporated after approval
            NOTHING

-- src:1235 | (D) the Secretary may approve after the date on which guidance is issued under subsection (a)(1);
@ref s 2016a(b)(1)(D) the Secretary may approve the plan after the date on which guidance is issued under subsection (a)(1) (src:1235)
GIVEN `the date of approval` IS A DATE
      `the date on which guidance is issued under subsection (a)(1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(1)(D) the Secretary may approve the plan` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF Day `the date of approval` GREATER THAN Day `the date on which guidance is issued under subsection (a)(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Secretary may approve after the date on which guidance is issued under subsection (a)(1)"
            -- note (a permission limited in time by its own wording; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            NOTHING

-- src:1242 | (3) plans approved under paragraph (1) will remain in effect until the effective date of the rule promulgated pursuant to subsection (a)(3); and
@ref s 2016a(b)(3) approved plans remain in effect until the effective date of the rule promulgated under subsection (a)(3) (src:1242)
-- In plain words: an approved plan stays in effect until the day the rule under (a)(3) takes effect. On that day the plan is no longer in effect (NOTES.md, fork F-2016a-2).
GIVEN `the plan was approved under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the effective date of the rule promulgated pursuant to subsection (a)(3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(3) the plan remains in effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the plan was approved under paragraph (1)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "plans approved under paragraph (1)"
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the effective date of the rule promulgated pursuant to subsection (a)(3)`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN JUST effective THEN
                    IF Day `the date on which the question is asked` LESS THAN Day effective
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE
                        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "will remain in effect until the effective date of the rule promulgated pursuant to subsection (a)(3)"
                        JUST FALSE

-- src:1243 | (4) replacements of benefits under this section shall not be regarded as losses for the purpose of section 2016(e) of this title to the extent such replacements are made in accordance with an approved plan that complies with this subsection.
@ref s 2016a(b)(4) replacements made in accordance with an approved plan that complies with this subsection are not regarded as losses for section 2016(e) (src:1243)
GIVEN `the replacement was made in accordance with an approved plan that complies with this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(b)(4) the replacement is regarded as a loss for the purpose of section 2016(e)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the replacement was made in accordance with an approved plan that complies with this subsection` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "replacements of benefits under this section shall not be regarded as losses for the purpose of section 2016(e) of this title to the extent such replacements are made in accordance with an approved plan that complies with this subsection"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent such replacements are made in accordance with an approved plan that complies with this subsection"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016a(c) definitions`

-- src:1244 | (c) Definitions
-- src:1245 | In this section, the terms “allotment”, “benefit”, “household”, “retail food store”, and “State agency” have the meaning given those terms in section 2012 of this title.
@ref s 2016a(c) allotment, benefit, household, retail food store and State agency have the meaning given in section 2012 (src:1244-1245)
-- The five terms are answered by section 2012, which is not in this part's text. This function checks that the three the replacement rule uses were all answered "yes" and says nothing more.
GIVEN `s 2012(d) the assistance is a benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(m) the individual or group is a household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(s) the body is a State agency` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(c) the terms used in this section have the meaning given in section 2012` MEANS
    `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST `s 2012(d) the assistance is a benefit`, `s 2012(m) the individual or group is a household`, `s 2012(s) the body is a State agency`)

§§ `s 2016a(d) rescission and (e) Comptroller General`

-- src:1246 | (d) Rescission
-- src:1247 | Of the unobligated balances made available for the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program as authorized by section 1101(b)(1) of the American Rescue Plan Act of 2021 (Public Law 117–2), $8,000,000 is hereby rescinded.
@ref s 2016a(d) of the unobligated balances of the American Rescue Plan Act program, $8,000,000 is rescinded (src:1246-1247)
GIVEN `the unobligated balances made available for the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program as authorized by section 1101(b)(1) of the American Rescue Plan Act of 2021, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2016a(d) the unobligated balances remaining after the rescission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the unobligated balances made available for the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program as authorized by section 1101(b)(1) of the American Rescue Plan Act of 2021, in dollars` AT LEAST `s 2016a(d) the amount of the unobligated balances rescinded, in dollars` THEN
            JUST (`the unobligated balances made available for the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program as authorized by section 1101(b)(1) of the American Rescue Plan Act of 2021, in dollars` MINUS `s 2016a(d) the amount of the unobligated balances rescinded, in dollars`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text rescinds $8,000,000 "of the unobligated balances" and does not say what is rescinded when the balances are smaller
            NOTHING

-- src:1250 | Not later than 1 year after September 26, 2024, the Comptroller General of the United States shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that examines risks related to supplemental nutrition assistance program electronic benefit transfer payment system security, including the risk of stolen benefits through card skimming, card cloning, and other similar methods.
@ref s 2016a(e)(1) the Comptroller General reports not later than 1 year after 26 September 2024 (src:1250)
GIVEN `the date on which the Comptroller General submitted the report` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(e)(1) the Comptroller General submitted the report in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the Comptroller General submitted the report`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no date was supplied, and whether the Comptroller General has submitted the report yet depends on today's date, which the text does not give
            NOTHING
        WHEN JUST submitted THEN
            IF Day submitted AT MOST Day `s 2016a(e)(1) the last day for the Comptroller General's report`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 1 year after September 26, 2024, the Comptroller General of the United States shall submit"
                JUST FALSE

-- src:1251 | (2) Contents
-- src:1252 | The report under paragraph (1) shall include an assessment of—
-- src:1253 | (A) the extent to which the Department of Agriculture manages payment system security, including risks related to stolen benefits, compared to leading industry practices;
-- src:1254 | (B) the manner in which States, retailers, and other relevant entities manage risks related to stolen benefits;
-- src:1255 | (C) the oversight of and guidance provided by the Secretary to States regarding stolen benefits; and
-- src:1256 | (D) recommendations and policy options for—
-- src:1257 | (i) improving how the Department of Agriculture and other relevant entities manage payment system security risks, including those related to stolen benefits; and
-- src:1258 | (ii) how the Department of Agriculture may best share those improvements with States, retailers, and other relevant entities.
@ref s 2016a(e)(2) the report includes an assessment of the four matters listed (src:1251-1258)
GIVEN `the report includes an assessment of the extent to which the Department of Agriculture manages payment system security, including risks related to stolen benefits, compared to leading industry practices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes an assessment of the manner in which States, retailers, and other relevant entities manage risks related to stolen benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes an assessment of the oversight of and guidance provided by the Secretary to States regarding stolen benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes an assessment of recommendations and policy options for improving how the Department of Agriculture and other relevant entities manage payment system security risks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes an assessment of recommendations and policy options for how the Department of Agriculture may best share those improvements with States, retailers, and other relevant entities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016a(e)(2) the report includes what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report includes an assessment of the extent to which the Department of Agriculture manages payment system security, including risks related to stolen benefits, compared to leading industry practices` AND `the report includes an assessment of the manner in which States, retailers, and other relevant entities manage risks related to stolen benefits` AND `the report includes an assessment of the oversight of and guidance provided by the Secretary to States regarding stolen benefits` AND `the report includes an assessment of recommendations and policy options for improving how the Department of Agriculture and other relevant entities manage payment system security risks` AND `the report includes an assessment of recommendations and policy options for how the Department of Agriculture may best share those improvements with States, retailers, and other relevant entities` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report under paragraph (1) shall include an assessment of"
            JUST FALSE
